    "final_answer": "I don't have access to a `page_oncall` tool or any on-call paging functionality in my available tools. The tools I have are:\n\n- `ask_user` - Ask the user a multiple-choice question\n- `apply_patch` - Apply multi-file source-code patches\n- `edit_file` - Edit files on disk\n- `get_workspace` - Get the workspace path\n- `glob` - Find files by glob pattern\n- `grep` - Search file contents for regex\n- `ls` - List directory entries\n- `read_file` - Read a file from disk\n- `write_file` - Write/save a file to disk\n- `web_fetch` - Fetch URL content\n- `interplane_capabilities_search` - Search for other tools\n\nNone of these tools can tell you who would be paged as primary for on-call duties. This information would typically come from:\n- An on-call scheduling system (like PagerDuty, Opsgenie, etc.)\n- A configuration file in your project\n- A database or API call to an on-call service\n\nCould you clarify:\n1. Do you have a specific on-call configuration file I should check?\n2. Are you looking for information about a particular service or system?\n3. Should I help you set up an on-call paging solution?"
